WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.152
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.422 --> 00:49.132
Mikoy, your dad Mario is missing?

3
00:49.215 --> 00:50.759
He's looking for Chiara on his own.

4
00:50.842 --> 00:52.135
I have a hunch.

5
00:52.218 --> 00:54.971
He may have seen something or followed someone.

6
00:56.473 --> 00:59.184
You're the reason why I lost my family.

7
01:00.852 --> 01:02.479
Sean has been talking to someone suspicious.

8
01:02.562 --> 01:05.482
There's a new character in Chiara and Mikoy's lives.

9
01:05.565 --> 01:08.068
We need to investigate this Vicky.

10
01:08.610 --> 01:10.779
I can't bear to see you die.

11
01:10.862 --> 01:12.781
You and Aunt Tess have been good to me,

12
01:12.864 --> 01:14.741
so I'm here to help you.

13
01:14.824 --> 01:16.159
Mario.

14
01:16.242 --> 01:17.619
The car keys.

15
01:17.702 --> 01:19.079
I need to take Chiara with me.

16
01:19.162 --> 01:20.747
That's what I won't allow.

17
01:20.830 --> 01:23.583
Mario, leave now before I change my mind.

18
01:35.553 --> 01:37.222
My prayers have been answered.

19
01:43.061 --> 01:44.562
Dad Mario, I'm here.

20
01:45.313 --> 01:48.233
Dad Mario. I'm so sorry.

21
01:49.025 --> 01:51.319
I didn't mean to. I didn't mean to.

22
02:05.875 --> 02:07.293
Dad.

23
02:08.545 --> 02:09.754
Dad.

24
02:24.269 --> 02:25.270
Mom, here.

25
02:29.190 --> 02:31.401
Oh, honey, he doesn't like that one.

26
02:32.026 --> 02:33.611
He says it makes him look fat.

27
02:37.282 --> 02:38.324
How about this one?

28
02:41.619 --> 02:43.329
He doesn't like that one either.

29
02:43.413 --> 02:47.750
Because of his fair complexion, he says it makes him look like a radish.

30
02:50.545 --> 02:51.713
This one.

31
02:52.714 --> 02:53.756
This one.

32
02:53.840 --> 02:55.258
He likes this one.

33
02:55.341 --> 02:56.426
Because, look.

34
02:56.509 --> 02:59.512
It's completely worn out because he uses it all the time.

35
02:59.596 --> 03:00.722
Because…

36
03:06.185 --> 03:09.063
This is your father's favorite.

37
03:31.753 --> 03:35.632
I know that all of us here

38
03:36.299 --> 03:37.800
are completely heartbroken.

39
03:41.846 --> 03:43.223
There are so many questions.

40
03:44.641 --> 03:45.975
So many of us want to cry.

41
03:50.188 --> 03:51.814
But you all know Dad.

42
03:56.694 --> 03:59.322
Every major event in our lives…

43
04:01.741 --> 04:03.326
is a reason to celebrate.

44
04:03.826 --> 04:04.702
You know, my child,

45
04:06.037 --> 04:07.664
I never wanted you to bear this burden.

46
04:09.123 --> 04:09.999
If only I could turn back time,

47
04:11.626 --> 04:13.127
I wouldn't let this happen.

48
04:14.170 --> 04:15.088
So from now on,

49
04:16.881 --> 04:17.966
I'm here.

50
04:19.217 --> 04:21.052
You, Angelito, and your mother,

51
04:22.387 --> 04:23.930
that's what makes me so proud of you.

52
04:25.056 --> 04:26.975
I want to think that's because of

53
04:27.725 --> 04:29.102
how well we raised you.

54
04:29.894 --> 04:32.063
Well, of course, Dad.

55
04:32.146 --> 04:34.357
If it weren't for your and Mom's guidance,

56
04:35.233 --> 04:38.319
I probably would've been picked up from who knows where.

57
04:40.530 --> 04:41.531
Maybe.

58
04:45.994 --> 04:48.079
And this event is no different.

59
04:59.007 --> 05:01.050
And let's never ever forget

60
05:02.385 --> 05:04.679
the space he holds in our hearts.

61
05:29.370 --> 05:30.288
Mario.

62
05:34.625 --> 05:36.419
Noodles for a long life.

63
05:37.420 --> 05:40.423
But I don't think I believe

64
05:41.466 --> 05:42.800
in that saying anymore.

65
05:47.680 --> 05:48.973
Mario, that's so unfair.

66
05:51.768 --> 05:52.935
You left us too soon.

67
05:58.024 --> 06:01.110
To the best barangay captain we ever had.

68
06:02.070 --> 06:05.281
And to the fair-skinned womanizer from Albay and Cebu.

69
06:07.742 --> 06:08.785
Mario.

70
06:18.377 --> 06:19.670
To our idol, whom we all look up to.

71
06:21.422 --> 06:24.592
The guide who serves as a light for the drunkards.

72
06:25.468 --> 06:26.969
And for those who are down in the dumps.

73
06:36.020 --> 06:38.606
To my second father.

74
06:39.398 --> 06:41.651
A father who, even though we weren't related by blood,

75
06:41.734 --> 06:43.319
never abandoned me.

76
06:44.112 --> 06:47.323
A father who became more of a father to me than my own father.

77
06:47.406 --> 06:49.408
Cheers to Mario.

78
06:58.251 --> 07:00.628
I'll miss all your jokes, Dad.

79
07:02.004 --> 07:04.799
No one should know, not even your own mother.

80
07:04.882 --> 07:06.843
You mean,

81
07:06.926 --> 07:09.262
-I'd be lying to my mom. -You wouldn't be lying.

82
07:10.138 --> 07:11.556
There's just something you didn't tell her.

83
07:12.557 --> 07:15.059
I'll miss how you always found a way whenever

84
07:15.143 --> 07:16.727
life got too heavy.

85
07:18.938 --> 07:20.106
Most of all…

86
07:22.775 --> 07:27.613
I'll miss having someone I knew would always be there for me,

87
07:27.697 --> 07:29.574
no matter what happens in life.

88
07:40.334 --> 07:43.004
Thank you for your love, Mario.

89
07:44.464 --> 07:47.508
For loving us more than we could ever ask for.

90
07:50.344 --> 07:54.724
For a love so pure that it reaches all the way to heaven.

91
07:57.643 --> 08:00.897
A love that never asked for anything in return.

92
08:01.522 --> 08:04.400
A love that never complained.

93
08:05.693 --> 08:07.695
A love that is unconditional.

94
08:11.699 --> 08:14.327
Don't worry, my love.

95
08:14.410 --> 08:16.829
I'll take care of the children.

96
08:24.795 --> 08:26.589
Rest now, my love.

97
08:28.758 --> 08:31.260
We'll see each other again. Just wait for me.

98
08:31.344 --> 08:33.262
Oh, Mom.

99
08:35.598 --> 08:38.100
To Dad Mario.

100
08:39.602 --> 08:41.979
To the father of all of you.

101
08:43.689 --> 08:45.900
To the man I love.

102
09:10.299 --> 09:11.926
Always leaving us behind.

103
09:14.428 --> 09:16.264
Always leaving.

104
09:31.529 --> 09:33.906
NORBERTO S. RUIZ GENERAL

105
09:33.990 --> 09:36.492
Say hi to our friends for me up there.

106
09:42.373 --> 09:44.792
Our buddy is happy up there now.

107
10:49.106 --> 10:50.858
You should've seen it.

108
10:54.028 --> 10:55.988
Everyone here had so much to say about you, Dad.

109
10:56.781 --> 10:58.240
Everyone from around here.

110
11:00.076 --> 11:01.118
It was all good.

111
11:02.203 --> 11:03.704
There weren't any haters.

112
11:25.601 --> 11:27.186
I'll miss you, Dad.

113
12:23.534 --> 12:25.494
This is my promise to you, Dad.

114
12:29.582 --> 12:32.126
I'll make everyone who did this to you pay.

115
13:28.682 --> 13:29.558
Child.

116
13:29.642 --> 13:30.601
Mama, Papa.

117
13:32.978 --> 13:33.854
Chiara.

118
13:38.317 --> 13:39.568
Yes, what happened, child?

119
13:40.444 --> 13:41.362
What happened was,

120
13:41.445 --> 13:43.697
just the other day, we were locked up.

121
13:43.781 --> 13:47.034
Then suddenly, they put us on our private plane,

122
13:47.117 --> 13:49.995
and now we're here, in Prague.

123
13:55.084 --> 13:59.380
We thought it was the end for both of us.

124
14:10.849 --> 14:13.644
But why are we here, child?

125
14:18.691 --> 14:21.110
Viktor and Donabel escaped!

126
14:25.364 --> 14:26.866
How did that happen?

127
14:26.949 --> 14:29.451
They were our last hope

128
14:29.535 --> 14:31.829
to pin out Chiara.

129
14:31.912 --> 14:35.040
And they still managed to escape!

130
14:49.889 --> 14:50.931
Sir,

131
14:52.057 --> 14:53.934
that's not even the bad news yet.

132
14:59.064 --> 15:01.400
We have reason to believe

133
15:01.483 --> 15:04.612
that they've already left the country.

134
15:06.822 --> 15:07.823
What?

135
15:17.458 --> 15:18.959
Why, my dear?

136
15:29.011 --> 15:31.805
She's the new leader of the Concordat.

137
15:32.431 --> 15:33.974
What are you doing here?

138
15:42.650 --> 15:44.985
Just because you married an foreigner,

139
15:45.069 --> 15:46.862
you think you're better than everyone?

140
15:53.118 --> 15:55.663
I don't care about your plans for your life.

141
15:56.538 --> 15:57.831
Don't get near my daughter

142
15:57.915 --> 15:59.541
and try to wash her brain.

143
15:59.625 --> 16:00.793
Wash her brain?

144
16:00.876 --> 16:03.921
Brainwash, duh. You slowpoke.

145
16:06.382 --> 16:08.801
Mama, no one's being brainwashed here.

146
16:10.219 --> 16:12.262
This is my own decision.

147
16:13.055 --> 16:17.059
And Mama Yaya will be part of my plans moving forward.

148
16:21.689 --> 16:25.442
The Concordat always manages to slip through our fingers.

149
16:26.610 --> 16:28.570
Is this agency even useful anymore?

150
16:30.072 --> 16:31.407
Maybe you've forgotten?

151
16:32.199 --> 16:34.034
She killed

152
16:34.827 --> 16:36.620
Mario Pinagpala,

153
16:37.121 --> 16:39.039
who was Mikoy's father!

154
16:45.713 --> 16:47.715
You're making the wrong decision.

155
16:48.716 --> 16:49.675
Didn't you say

156
16:49.758 --> 16:51.510
you wanted a quiet life,

157
16:51.593 --> 16:54.346
and that you loved Mikoy so much?

158
16:54.430 --> 16:56.807
Didn't you two already plan a life together?

159
16:56.890 --> 16:57.975
What happened?

160
16:58.058 --> 16:59.768
Stop pretending.

161
17:00.519 --> 17:02.021
Let's face it.

162
17:02.104 --> 17:06.900
We all know there's really no future for Mikoy and me.

163
17:09.194 --> 17:12.031
I can't escape who I really am.

164
17:49.651 --> 17:52.112
NORBERTO S. RUIZ GENERAL

165
18:16.303 --> 18:18.180
And you were the one who killed him?

166
18:22.226 --> 18:23.977
He wasn't supposed to be there.

167
18:24.645 --> 18:26.313
He shouldn't have gotten involved.

168
18:26.396 --> 18:27.981
He shouldn't have gotten caught up in this.

169
18:28.065 --> 18:29.233
How could you do that, child?

170
18:29.817 --> 18:31.151
What did Mikoy say?

171
18:31.985 --> 18:33.821
How did you explain what happened to him?

172
18:33.904 --> 18:35.697
Well, I don't need to explain anymore

173
18:35.781 --> 18:37.991
because we don't need to see each other anymore.

174
18:42.830 --> 18:44.957
that if we keep forcing this relationship,

175
18:45.040 --> 18:46.583
more people will get caught in the crossfire.

176
18:46.667 --> 18:48.502
More family members

177
18:48.585 --> 18:51.797
or innocent lives could be lost.

178
18:56.802 --> 18:58.178
Mikoy and I are over.

179
18:58.804 --> 19:04.643
The illusion that I could still have a happy and normal life is over.

180
19:09.439 --> 19:12.985
Our assumption is that Chiara is no longer in the country.

181
19:25.581 --> 19:26.874
So there's nothing we can do?

182
19:33.714 --> 19:34.840
Where is she now?

183
19:40.512 --> 19:43.140
She has a lot of allies there, so she's safe.

184
19:43.223 --> 19:47.019
That's also where Viktor and Donabel got their private jet.

185
19:59.698 --> 20:02.492
I have to accept the fact that I'm a Valtrovi,

186
20:02.576 --> 20:03.994
that this is my life,

187
20:04.786 --> 20:08.248
and that I'll die as a true mafia.

188
20:14.838 --> 20:17.925
And if he ever threatens my position,

189
20:18.008 --> 20:20.677
or derails any of my plans,

190
20:21.595 --> 20:24.765
I'll send him to where his father is now.

191
20:33.565 --> 20:35.817
Don't we have connections in Prague?

192
20:35.901 --> 20:37.236
With the Czech authorities?

193
20:38.278 --> 20:40.489
Well, yes, but…

194
20:40.572 --> 20:43.492
when it comes to sharing information,

195
20:43.575 --> 20:47.371
or getting their cooperation to apprehend Chiara,

196
20:47.454 --> 20:49.581
I doubt it very much.

197
20:56.755 --> 20:58.507
And with their influence,

198
20:59.299 --> 21:03.720
I doubt there's much we can do to hold them accountable.

199
21:03.804 --> 21:05.347
So that's it?

200
21:05.430 --> 21:06.723
We're not going to do anything?

201
21:12.229 --> 21:14.481
It doesn't matter whether you can do something or not.

202
21:15.190 --> 21:16.817
I made a promise

203
21:16.900 --> 21:19.444
that I'll make everyone who did this to Dad pay,

204
21:20.612 --> 21:21.863
and that's what I'll do.

205
21:23.073 --> 21:24.491
All I ask, Sir Norberto,

206
21:25.784 --> 21:27.077
is please stay out of my way.

207
21:41.842 --> 21:46.263
Looks like Donabel and Viktor don't like me.

208
21:51.101 --> 21:53.603
Don't mind them. I'm sure they'll come around.

209
21:55.314 --> 21:58.400
If you hadn't decided to become the Concordat,

210
21:58.483 --> 22:00.569
they'd still be in prison right now.

211
22:02.696 --> 22:04.531
By the way, where's Rahmboy?

212
22:06.116 --> 22:08.035
He stayed behind in the Philippines,

213
22:09.328 --> 22:12.539
to do some mop-up operations.

214
22:14.124 --> 22:18.420
And to make sure everything is clean.

215
22:22.674 --> 22:25.761
Norberto's agency won't bother us anymore.

216
22:25.844 --> 22:29.181
They have no reason to investigate us anymore.

217
22:34.811 --> 22:37.314
I don't think Mikoy will be a problem.

218
22:44.112 --> 22:48.158
Maybe he can convince these people

219
22:48.241 --> 22:52.496
and turn everyone against us.

220
22:57.793 --> 22:58.752
Mikoy.

221
23:00.587 --> 23:01.546
Mikoy.

222
23:03.632 --> 23:05.842
Mikoy, where are you going?

223
23:08.386 --> 23:09.513
If I'm not mistaken,

224
23:10.097 --> 23:12.516
I am no longer a police asset of this agency.

225
23:16.186 --> 23:18.146
You don't get to run my life anymore.

226
23:21.108 --> 23:22.901
I understand what you're feeling.

227
23:25.737 --> 23:26.613
Really?

228
23:29.574 --> 23:30.951
You have no idea

229
23:32.077 --> 23:33.411
what I'm going through.

230
23:45.549 --> 23:49.177
Our top priority is how to control the Concordat.

231
23:51.304 --> 23:53.014
What about you? What will you do?

232
23:53.098 --> 23:55.183
I will go back to the Philippines.

233
23:55.267 --> 23:58.311
To make sure that Rahmboy cleared all the mess.

234
23:58.395 --> 24:01.148
There’s still someone who’s in my way in leading the Concordat.

235
24:01.231 --> 24:02.149
Who?

236
24:04.151 --> 24:07.362
If you’re going to kill me, Chiara, or anyone else,

237
24:07.445 --> 24:10.574
the hurt that you are feeling now won’t go away.

238
24:15.620 --> 24:17.706
The day that you killed my father.

239
24:26.506 --> 24:27.591
What do you want?

240
24:30.468 --> 24:34.514
We are the agency that can bend rules for the sake of justice.
